  <amendment date="2026-07-18" by="spaarkeai-compose-r3 re-architecture">
    EXPANDED scope + Option C. Two changes:
    (1) DROP the "Approach A cosmetic re-serialization acceptable" allowance in the prose below — under
        Option C (`ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer`) untouched paragraphs are BYTE-IDENTICAL (amended
        FR-07). Assert byte-identity for untouched paragraphs, not merely structural equivalence.
    (2) ADD a SECOND seam path — BORN-IN-EDITOR creation: POST a paraId-keyed content model through
        `create-on-save`, capture the SERVER-RENDERED bytes (026 `ComposeDocumentRenderer`) at the
        SpeFileStore facade, and assert the rendered `.docx` is well-formed, round-trips through the Load
        import + `ParaIdPreParser`, carries a unique `w14:paraId` per paragraph, and — the numbering
        GOLDEN-FILE — renders a 1/1.1/1.1.1 clause tree as a style-linked multi-level `abstractNum`. Also
        assert a subsequent tracked-change edit on the rendered doc does not corrupt its numbering.
    Deps now include 026 (renderer) + 027 (client cutover) so the seam exercises the real end-to-end path.
  </amendment>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-07 + NFR-06: a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test in
    `tests/integration/seam/**` that proves the E1 fidelity guarantee end-to-end. The test drives the
    real save route with an edited formatted `.docx` and asserts that untouched paragraphs preserve
    their text, `w14:paraId`, styles, numbering, headers/footers, footnotes, and (nested) tables — while
    the edited paragraphs show the edits (as tracked changes). This is the E2E Definition-of-Done proof
    for the E1 cutover: unit-green ≠ done. TEST-MODIFYING task — code-review + adr-check run at Step 9.5
    UNCONDITIONALLY. Mock ONLY at the `SpeFileStore` facade boundary; NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`,
    NO DI-registration/ctor-null tests (ADR-038).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 test engineer fluent in `WebApplicationFactory` through-the-wire seam tests and Open
    XML assertion (reading `w:p`/`w14:paraId`/`w:pStyle`/`w:numPr`/headers/footers/footnotes/tables from
    the persisted `.docx`). Follows the repo's `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice conventions and
    the ADR-038 mock-boundary rules (mock only the SPE facade; the HTTP boundary is real).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A seam slice test under `tests/integration/seam/` that: POSTs an edit to a formatted-doc fixture
    through the real save route (post-022 delta path); captures the persisted bytes at the SpeFileStore
    facade boundary; and asserts (a) untouched paragraphs preserve text + `w14:paraId` + `pStyle` +
    numbering + headers/footers + footnotes + (nested) tables; (b) the edited paragraphs carry the edits
    as tracked changes. The test fails if a dirty save degrades any untouched structure (regression
    guard for the fidelity invariant).</goal>

