  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context check">Confirm tasks 022 + 023 are complete (the delta save + AI-annotation composition under test). Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (TEST-MODIFYING → gates unconditional). Read the seam README + existing Compose seam test.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Build the formatted-doc fixture">Create/obtain a formatted `.docx` fixture with a letterhead header/footer, multi-level clause numbering, custom styles, footnotes, and a (nested) table — with stable `w14:paraId`s. Reuse an S1/S1b fixture where possible.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author the seam test">Under `tests/integration/seam/`, stand up `WebApplicationFactory` with the SpeFileStore facade faked (capture persisted bytes). POST an edit (edit ~3 paragraphs incl. one run-format change) through the real save route with the body the client sends. Capture the persisted `.docx`.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Assert fidelity">Open the persisted bytes with the Open XML SDK; assert untouched paragraphs preserve text + `w14:paraId` + `pStyle` + numbering; assert headers/footers, footnotes, and (nested) tables are intact; assert the edited paragraphs carry the edits (tracked changes). Allow cosmetic re-serialization (Approach A).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify">Run the seam test (green); run the full seam suite for no regression. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

