  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A `WebApplicationFactory` seam test POSTs an edit to a formatted-doc fixture through the real save route and captures the persisted bytes at the SpeFileStore facade boundary (not a service-level unit test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test asserts untouched paragraphs preserve text + `w14:paraId` + styles (`pStyle`) + numbering + headers/footers + footnotes + (nested) tables after edit+save.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test asserts the edited paragraphs carry the edits as tracked changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test uses no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration test, no ctor-null test; it mocks only at the SpeFileStore facade and lives under `tests/integration/seam/**`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cosmetic re-serialization (BOM/whitespace, Approach A) does not fail the test; structural/semantic equivalence is asserted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seam test passes and the full seam suite has no regression.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

